From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:54:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Tick several worlds on one thread: a world joins another's
 thread and leaves it alone

AthenaWorldThread ticks a list of worlds. WorldServer.athenaJoinThread puts a
world on the thread that ticks another, so players and entities move between
them at once and one thread owns both; athenaStopThread on a world that shares
its thread takes that world off at the end of a tick (or, if the thread is
stuck, once it gets there) and leaves the thread to the others. Tasks are
tagged with their world and follow a world that left. The watchdog, the
world-stopped section for vanilla commands and the failure handling work per
thread; a thread that throws halts all its worlds. An unload that gives up
puts the world back on its thread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

